<newsitem itemid="44485" id="root" date="1996-09-10" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Amstrad makes 14.9 million stg loss in year. [CORRECTED 09:40 GMT]</title>
<headline>Amstrad makes 14.9 million stg loss in year. [CORRECTED 09:40 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) adjusted   8.6 loss	     vs 1.3 earnings</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.5		    vs 1.5</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 2.75		   vs 2.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     14.9 loss	    vs 3.1 profit</p>
<p> Turnover		   329.3		  vs 271.6</p>
<p> Operating result	 14.93 loss	   vs 5.16 loss</p>
<p> Interest receivable    6.3		    vs 7.2</p>
<p> (Corrects to show interest was received not paid. Corrects figures from 6.24 vs 7.21)</p>
<p> Tax			  0.68		   vs 0.46</p>
<p> Net taxed		  15.63 loss	   vs 2.59 profit</p>
<p> Attributable	     16.03 loss	   vs 2.53 profit</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 1</p>
<p> Div registration date  September 24</p>
<p> Ex-div date		September 16</p>
<p>NOTE - Amstrad Plc said results included restructuring and redundancy costs of 10.7 million stg for its consumer electronics business.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
